  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></math></p><p> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>We know that, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is positive for all real numbers, now it depends on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>. </p><p>So,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>is increasing if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>></mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is decreasing if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo> </mo><mi>x</mi><mo><</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mo>∞</mo></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>∞</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mo>∞</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>∞</mo></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/198400f3-f157-4996-b111-8d81fdd8a2fe-image.png\"/></p><p>So, it is clear that graph cuts the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis at two points, so number of solutions are two.</p>",
